    {
      "id": 233777,
      "name": "catDreaming",
      "username": "catDreaming",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/4491bb/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2020-10-05T17:22:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>To actually put the card text:</p>\n<p>\"Defend 1 per Dahan.<br>\nDahan in target land cannot be changed.<br>\n<em>( When they would be damaged, destroed, removed, replaced, or moved, don't. )</em>\"</p>\n<p>Seems pretty straightforward to me. When Stubborn Solidity activates, you count the number of Dahan in that land, and Defend that land for that much until the turn ends. At the same time, that land gains 'Dahan in this land cannot be changed' as specified on the card until end of turn. Nothing stops Dahan from being added to the land.</p>",
      "post_number": 15,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:09:41.596Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
